# Generated from: specs/299-remove-completed-execute-runtime-checkpoints/requirements.md
Feature: Remove completed execute runtime checkpoints
  A successful queue must release only its runtime ownership so a new queue can start.
  Nonterminal queues retain resumable state, and unsafe cleanup fails closed.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Fully completed queue removes exact run-owned runtime
    Given a bound execute queue whose issues completed every delivery step
    And exact issue-step handoffs, worker-step provenance, and unrelated runtime files exist
    When the controller finalizes the queue
    Then its checkpoint, exact handoffs, and worker provenance are absent
    And unrelated runtime files remain

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Different issue starts after completed cleanup
    Given a prior differently identified queue completed and cleanup succeeded
    When the controller starts an eligible new issue
    Then no stale checkpoint identity mismatch is returned
    And the new run establishes its own checkpoint identity

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Nonterminal queue retains resumable runtime
    Given a bound queue is <state>
    When the controller stops before full successful delivery
    Then its checkpoint and supporting runtime files remain

    Examples:
      | state       |
      | interrupted |
      | failed      |
      | blocked     |

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Unsafe completed cleanup fails closed
    Given a fully completed queue whose cleanup has <hazard>
    When final cleanup is attempted
    Then the controller fails with completed_cleanup_failed
    And it does not report successful finalization

    Examples:
      | hazard             |
      | a held lock         |
      | an identity mismatch|
      | a symlink boundary  |
      | a deletion failure  |

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Runtime tracking stays ignored and untracked
    Given execute runtime files exist under .omp/sdlc/
    When Git ignore and index state are inspected
    Then the runtime files are ignored
    And no runtime file is tracked
